    "reasoning": "The variant is located within the TP53 gene on chromosome 17 and is annotated on transcript ENST00000269305. It is described as substitution.\n\nThe submitted variant TP53:c.743G>A was evaluated using multiple publicly available genomic resources including Ensembl, ClinVar, HGVS validation and the educational ACMG-inspired evidence engine.\n\nThis interpretation is primarily supported by the ClinVar clinical significance of 'Pathogenic'. The available record has a review status of 'reviewed by expert panel', providing additional confidence in the submitted interpretation.\n\nEnsembl predicts a missense variant. Missense substitutions alter a single amino acid but their biological impact depends on the affected residue and protein domain. Additional functional or computational evidence would normally be required.\n\nBased on the currently available evidence, this educational ACMG-inspired framework classifies the variant as Likely Pathogenic.\n\nThe available evidence supports a likely pathogenic interpretation, although additional clinical and functional evidence would further strengthen confidence.\n\nThis report is intended exclusively for educational and research purposes and must not be used for clinical diagnosis or medical decision making.",
